No runtime, worker, lifecycle, request, stream, config, router, backend adapter, execution descriptor, bus execute-action, scheduler, public API, or native/model execution files were modified.

---

## 4. Modular design shape

The new namespace is intentionally split into small contract modules:

```text
modelBundleCommon.mjs        shared constants, copy helpers, field/key/path guard helpers
modelBundleDefinition.mjs    single bundle validation/normalization/assert helpers
modelBundleRegistry.mjs      registry validation, creation, listing, lookup helpers
modelBundleContract.mjs      thin re-export barrel
```

`runtime/models/` is a metadata contract namespace, not a runtime loader and not a backend execution namespace.

---

## 5. Contract behavior

The new contract exposes:

```js
validateModelBundleDefinition(bundle)
normalizeModelBundleDefinition(bundle)
assertModelBundleDefinition(bundle)
validateModelBundleRegistry(registry)
normalizeModelBundleRegistry(registry)
assertModelBundleRegistry(registry)
createModelBundleRegistry(bundles)
listModelBundles(registry)
getModelBundle(registry, bundleId)
hasModelBundle(registry, bundleId)
listModelBundlesForCapability(registry, capability)
listModelBundlesForBackendKind(registry, backendKind)
```

Bundle definitions include:

```text
bundleId
status
label
capabilities
backendKind
backendId
defaultHardwareProfileId
artifactLayout
requirements
metadata
```

Supported artifact layout kinds:

```text
gguf-text
gguf-mmproj
hf-multimodal
server-managed
native-vision
```

`defaultHardwareProfileId` is validated only as a metadata string in this branch. Hardware profile schema and existence validation remain future work.

---

## 6. Guardrails preserved

The branch preserves these boundaries:

```text
runtime.mjs public export set unchanged
prompt() behavior unchanged
workerBridge unchanged
llama_worker unchanged
runtime/config unchanged
configOverride unchanged
scheduler unchanged
request lifecycle unchanged
stream shaping unchanged
runtime/router unchanged
runtime/backends unchanged
runtime/execution unchanged
runtime/bus/executeAction unchanged
```

The new modules avoid imports of:

```text
runtime.mjs
workerBridge
llama_worker
node-llama-cpp
worker_threads
child_process
runtime lifecycle modules
runtime request modules
runtime stream modules
```

The contract allows artifact reference metadata only inside `artifactLayout`. Request/execution payload keys remain rejected, including:

```text
backendOptions
adapterArgs
rawBackendPayload
toolProcess
command
shell
exec
spawn
cwd
env
function
handler
execute
executeAction
invoke
workerBridge
llama_worker
nodeLlamaCpp
configOverride
```

Path-like values outside `artifactLayout` are rejected.

